# Mission A: the EKF takes EVERY source from the LIO.  No GPS, no compass, no barometer.
#
# BASIS: this file is the old project's `sim/config/apm_real_drone.parm`, which was generated from the
# real aircraft's own parameter list and checked line by line against the FCU's live parameter names
# (docs/COMPONENTS.md section 10).  Its five-source block is the configuration the real drone flies.
# What is NEW here (and stated as such) is listed under "DEVIATIONS" at the bottom.
#
# HOW TO USE
#   sim_vehicle.py ... --defaults <copter defaults>,<airframe>,<this file>   (this file LAST, it wins)
#   and ALWAYS with WIPE_EEPROM=1: SITL's eeprom.bin overrides --defaults at boot, which is how
#   VISO_TYPE silently stayed 0 through several attempts in the old project.
#
# FORMAT: ArduPilot parm files do NOT support trailing comments -- a "#" after a value invalidates it.
# Every comment sits on its own line.
#
# ============================================ EKF core
AHRS_EKF_TYPE 3
EK3_ENABLE 1
EK3_PRIMARY 0
EK3_IMU_MASK 3
EK3_AFFINITY 0
EK3_SRC_OPTIONS 0

# ==================================== vision odometry (the LIO)
# VISO_TYPE 1 = the MAVLink backend.  Without it AP_VisualOdom::enabled() is false and
# AP_NavEKF_Source::pre_arm_check() blocks arming with "EK3 sources require VisualOdom".
VISO_TYPE 1
VISO_DELAY_MS 10
VISO_POS_M_NSE 0.2
VISO_VEL_M_NSE 0.1
VISO_YAW_M_NSE 0.2
VISO_QUAL_MIN 0
VISO_ORIENT 0
VISO_SCALE 1
VISO_POS_X 0
VISO_POS_Y 0
VISO_POS_Z 0

# THE ACCURACY CONTRACT.  A visual velocity more than EK3_VIS_VERR_MAX from the EKF's own estimate is
# REJECTED, so this number is what "the LIO must be accurate enough" means in metres per second.
# The old project added it while the EKF was fusing a velocity uncorrelated with real motion
# (correlation -0.048).  Do not loosen it to make a bad odometry fly.
EK3_VIS_VERR_MAX 0.9
EK3_VIS_VERR_MIN 0.1

# =================== ALL FIVE SOURCES FROM THE LIO
# YAW=6 is the important one: the EKF ADOPTS the LIO's heading instead of cross-checking it against a
# compass, which is why no frame alignment is needed anywhere -- and why the old project's +-180 deg
# "alignment" was the bug rather than the fix.  Consequence to remember when reading the logs: the
# absolute orientation of the LIO's world is arbitrary; only its shape matters.
EK3_SRC1_POSXY 6
EK3_SRC1_VELXY 6
EK3_SRC1_POSZ 6
EK3_SRC1_VELZ 6
EK3_SRC1_YAW 6
EK3_SRC2_POSXY 6
EK3_SRC2_VELXY 6
EK3_SRC2_POSZ 6
EK3_SRC2_VELZ 6
EK3_SRC2_YAW 6
EK3_SRC3_POSXY 6
EK3_SRC3_VELXY 6
EK3_SRC3_POSZ 6
EK3_SRC3_VELZ 6
EK3_SRC3_YAW 6

# ============================================ EKF tuning (the old project's verified block)
EK3_ABIAS_P_NSE 0.02
EK3_ACC_BIAS_LIM 1.0
EK3_ACC_P_NSE 0.35
EK3_ALT_M_NSE 2.0
EK3_BETA_MASK 0
EK3_CHECK_SCALE 100
EK3_ERR_THRESH 0.2
EK3_FLOW_USE 1
EK3_GBIAS_P_NSE 0.001
EK3_GLITCH_RAD 25
EK3_GND_EFF_DZ 4.0
EK3_GSF_RST_MAX 2
EK3_GSF_RUN_MASK 3
EK3_GSF_USE_MASK 3
EK3_GYRO_P_NSE 0.015
EK3_HGT_DELAY 60
EK3_HGT_I_GATE 500
EK3_HRT_FILT 2.0
EK3_MAGB_P_NSE 0.0001
EK3_MAGE_P_NSE 0.001
EK3_MAG_CAL 3
EK3_MAG_EF_LIM 50
EK3_MAG_I_GATE 300
EK3_MAG_MASK 0
EK3_MAG_M_NSE 0.05
EK3_NOAID_M_NSE 10.0
EK3_OGN_HGT_MASK 0
EK3_POSNE_M_NSE 0.5
EK3_POS_I_GATE 500
EK3_RNG_USE_HGT -1
EK3_RNG_USE_SPD 2.0
EK3_TAU_OUTPUT 25
EK3_VELD_M_NSE 0.5
EK3_VELNE_M_NSE 0.3
EK3_VEL_I_GATE 500
EK3_WIND_PSCALE 1.0
EK3_WIND_P_NSE 0.2
EK3_YAW_I_GATE 300
EK3_YAW_M_NSE 0.5

# ==================================== sensors the aircraft does not have
COMPASS_USE 0
COMPASS_USE2 0
COMPASS_USE3 0

# ============================================ filters
INS_GYRO_FILTER 20
INS_ACCEL_FILTER 20
INS_HNTCH_ENABLE 0

# ================================= failsafe / guided
FS_EKF_THRESH 1.0
GUID_TIMEOUT 3.0
# 8 = bit3 SetAttitudeTarget_ThrustAsThrust.  With 0 the SET_ATTITUDE_TARGET thrust field means CLIMB
# RATE, so an attitude controller sending "0.55 thrust" climbs forever.  The old project settled on 8.
GUID_OPTIONS 8

# ============================================================
# DEVIATIONS FROM THE OLD PROJECT'S FILE (each one deliberate)
# ============================================================
# Old sim kept GPS so it could use the FCU's own solution as truth.  We do not need that any more --
# the truth comes from the SITL tap -- so mission A is flown with NO GPS AT ALL, which is what
# "the EKF source is the LIO" means.  Side effect: the EKF ORIGIN MUST BE SET EXPLICITLY, because
# without GPS ArduPilot cannot derive it; the FSM sends SET_GPS_GLOBAL_ORIGIN once after the LIO is
# live (the old project never exercised this: docs/MEASUREMENTS.md says so in as many words).
GPS1_TYPE 0
SIM_GPS1_TYPE 0

# Arming: the vision (VISO) check must stay enabled; GPS / compass / baro checks are skipped because
# the aircraft does not carry them.  The old project used exactly this mask, with the real drone's
# ARMING_CHECK 798192 as its inverted twin.  VERIFY THE BITS against this firmware's AP_Arming.h
# before flying (see docs/PLAN.md rule 3: a parameter change must be verified to have reached the
# consumer -- a wrong mask here silently arms a vehicle whose EKF has no position).
ARMING_SKIPCHK 250382

# Waypoint/loiter speeds and accelerations from the real aircraft (the old file's rename map).
ATC_ANGLE_MAX 30.0
LAND_ALT_LOW_M 10.0
LAND_SPD_MS 0.5
LOIT_ACC_MAX_M 5.0
LOIT_BRK_ACC_M 2.5
LOIT_BRK_JRK_M 5.0
LOIT_SPEED_MS 12.5
PILOT_ACC_Z 2.5
PILOT_SPD_DN 0.0
PILOT_SPD_UP 2.5
RTL_ALT_M 15.0
WP_ACC 2.5
WP_ACC_Z 1.0
WP_JERK 1.0
WP_RFND_USE 1
WP_SPD 10.0
WP_SPD_DN 1.5
WP_SPD_UP 2.5
WP_TER_MARGIN 10.0
WP_RADIUS_M 0.5
LOIT_BRK_DELAY 1.0
PILOT_Y_RATE 202.5

# ============================================================================
# WHAT MUST **NOT** BE IN THIS FILE
# ============================================================================
# Any ATC_RAT_* rate gain.  Measured in the old project: copying the real aircraft's gains silently
# overrode the simulation airframe's damping profile, the roll-rate loop limit-cycled at |R-RDes|
# median 22 deg/s (max 34.6) and the vehicle TUMBLED at t=133 s, while the flight that did not load
# those gains tracked to 0.1 deg/s.  Rate gains describe an airframe; this file describes a source map.
#
# ============================================================================
# PREREQUISITE BEFORE FLYING MISSION A (measured, not a worry)
# ============================================================================
# EK3_SRC1_POSZ=6 means the ALTITUDE LOOP eats the LIO's z.  The old project had to fall back to the
# barometer (POSZ 1 / VELZ 0) in simulation because the LIO's height was "~0.9 m off five seconds
# after arming, then running away", and after landing the altitude datum walked off to -12 m.
#
# Our round-7 measurements (docs/GPS-VALIDATION-PIPELINE.md, ROUND 7) show the LIO's vertical is good
# -- 31-37 mm rms as scored, 1.9-2.2 mm once one rigid rotation is allowed -- but that rotation is a
# 2.35-2.61 deg PITCH of the whole estimate, and a pitch error of theta costs theta * horizontal
# distance in height: at 2.5 deg that is 43 mm per metre of travel.  Over the 2.0 m leg of the square
# the FCU would see a phantom 86 mm climb and chase it.
#
# So: FIND AND FIX THE 2.5 deg BEFORE TRUSTING POSZ=6.  It is the one open defect from the old work
# (injected within a second of liftoff, initialisation is provably clean: parked ground-truth attitude
# error 0.001 deg).  If it cannot be fixed quickly, mission A can still be flown with POSZ 1 (baro
# height) / VELZ 0 while keeping the horizontal channels on the LIO -- that is a documented,
# deliberate fallback, not a silent one.
